This repository contains no OM Digital Solutions / Olympus firmware. The patcher (firmware/patch.py) works on the
official firmware file that each user downloads themselves; releases/*/patch.json hold only the bytes this project writes
(its own code, hooks and pointers to that code).

Based on Caduceus (cakelesscoder/caduceus-ep7, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 cakelesscoder), firmware patches for the
Olympus PEN E-P7: the on-camera look editor design, the BUNDLES.BIN slot layout (firmware/vendor/
caduceus-bundles-layout.json), the tone-curve model and base LUT in the Look Lab (looklab/data.js, ported from its
webapp), the 29 starter colour looks in the Look Lab, the Look Lab's importer for Caduceus look codes, pack links and LOOKS.BIN
(ported from its webapp/src/sharecode.ts, pack.ts and format.ts), and the official-firmware download request in patch.py.

Test photos in looklab/samples are public domain (CC0 1.0); see looklab/samples/CREDITS.md.

The Look Lab embeds "OM3 Label Condensed", a renamed ASCII subset of DejaVu Sans Condensed (Bitstream Vera licence;
DejaVu changes public domain), to draw profile-name pictures; see looklab/FONT-LICENSE.txt.

Developer tools in tools/emulator drive om-emu (github.com/flatpanda/om-emu), which is not included and keeps its
own licence.

"OM SYSTEM", "Olympus" and "OM-3" are trademarks of their owners, as are the film names used for the starter looks
(Fujifilm, Kodak and others). The looks are interpretations, not the manufacturers' own. Not affiliated with OM Digital
